# Frontend Development Patterns (Streamlit)

## Application Structure
- **Main App**: @frontend/main.py - Entry point and navigation
- **Pages**: @frontend/pages - Role-specific pages
- **Utils**: @frontend/utils - Shared utilities and components
- **Session State**: Use `st.session_state` for user data persistence

## UI/UX Patterns
- **Role-based Interface**: Different UI for Learner, Instructor, and Admin
- **Page Navigation**: Implement role-based page routing
- **Loading States**: Show loading indicators for async operations
- **Error Handling**: Display user-friendly error messages
- **Responsive Design**: Ensure interface works on different screen sizes

## Data Handling
- **API Integration**: Use requests library for backend communication
- **Data Validation**: Validate user inputs before sending to backend
- **Caching**: Implement caching for frequently accessed data
- **File Uploads**: Handle file uploads with proper validation

## Security & Performance
- **Authentication**: Implement proper login/logout flow
- **Role Verification**: Check user roles before displaying sensitive content
- **Lazy Loading**: Load data only when needed
- **Efficient Rendering**: Minimize unnecessary re-renders